    "mapping_notes": "# .\n\n## Reference interface\n\nAll indices below are logical indices. Byte-level layout information from the\nsaved optimized input is retained in source_interface.\n\n| Parameter | Type | Logical shape | Role | Optimized counterpart |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Q | bf16 | 9 x 6 x 255 x 256 | input | Q (tensor map, parameter 5) |\n| K | bf16 | 9 x 6 x 256 x 256 | input | K (tensor map, parameter 6) |\n| V | bf16 | 9 x 6 x 256 x 256 | input | V (tensor map, parameter 7) |\n| O | bf16 | 9 x 6 x 255 x 256 | output | O (TMA-store tensor map, parameter 8) |\n| scale_log2 | float | 0.09016843885183334 | input | scale_log2 (parameter 9) |\n| LSE | float | 9 x 6 x 255 | output | LSE (pointer, parameter 4) |\n\n## Computation and mapping\n\nScenario: tests/cute/test_flash_attn.py::test_flash_attn_output, first hd256 row of the (255, 256) pair, which upstream labels \"SM100 hd256 2CTA test case\"\n(seqlen_q = 255, seqlen_k = 256, d = dv = 256, MHA, batch 9, 6 heads, bf16, non-causal).\nQ[b,h,q,d], K[b,kh,k,d], and V[b,kh,k,v] are the logical tensors.\nkh = floor(h / (query_heads / kv_heads)) = h (MHA).\nscore[k] = scale_log2 * sum_d Q[b,h,q,d] * K[b,kh,k,d].\nO = sum_k 2^(score[k]-max(score)) * V[k] / sum_k 2^(score[k]-max(score)).\nLSE[b,h,q] = ln(sum_k 2^score[k]) (kernel: (rowmax * scale_log2 + log2(rowsum)) * ln 2).\nscale_log2 = f32(1/sqrt(256)) * f32(log2 e), computed by the host launcher; no descale tensors.\nQ, K and O tensor-map coordinates are [d,s,h,b]; V uses the transposed view (d,s,h,b) with d contiguous.\nThe torch tensors are contiguous (b,s,h,d); the right-side strides restate that storage in (b,h,s,d) order.\nO is written by the TMA store through parameter 8; there is no output pointer parameter.\nLSE is the contiguous torch (b,h,s) float32 tensor; the kernel addresses it through the (s,h,b) view\nwith element strides (1, 255, 1530) read from parameter 4 (+24 and +32).\n\n## Validation boundary\n\nNot compared against an optimized GPU execution.\nPrecision/reduction-order differences follow\nthe mathematical contract in the top-level README.\n\n## Upstream\n\n- https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/blob/98c1cee0ed59307833841cdbf567fe336ceec13a/flash_attn/cute/flash_fwd_sm100.py\n- https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/blob/98c1cee0ed59307833841cdbf567fe336ceec13a/flash_attn/cute/interface.py\n- https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/blob/98c1cee0ed59307833841cdbf567fe336ceec13a/flash_attn/cute/tile_scheduler.py\n- https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/blob/98c1cee0ed59307833841cdbf567fe336ceec13a/flash_attn/cute/testing.py\n- https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/blob/98c1cee0ed59307833841cdbf567fe336ceec13a/tests/cute/test_flash_attn.py\n"
  },
